  <para style="h">Ñwed Mbon Kalesia</para>
  <para style="toc1">Ñwed Mbon Kalesia</para>
  <para style="toc2">Ñwed Mbon Kalesia</para>
  <para style="toc3">Kal</para>
  <para style="mt1">Ñwed Mbon Kalesia</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="GAL 1" />
  <para style="s1">Ekọọm Pọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="GAL 1:1" />Ado ami Pọọl abọsịd e-esioho edọñ, idooho mme awo inyʌññọ ido awo ndomokeed andọñ, ado Yisọs Krais ye Abasi Ete, a-akenamma anye aset ke ñkpa, <verse eid="GAL 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="GAL 1:2" />ye afịd mme nditọeka<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek adelfọi a-adaaha anọ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nditọeka </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ideen me ibaan</char><char style="ft" closed="false">anyʌñ ada anọ ideen ye ibaan e-enịmme Krais ke akpanikọ, ke atu ubon Abasi; se ñko ke Kalesia 1:11; Kalesia 3:15; Kalesia 4:12, 28, 31; Kalesia 5:11, 13; Kalesia 6:1, 18</char></note> ke Krais e-ebaaha ye ami, inọọ ñwed ami esọk mme ufọkabasi ke Kalesia.<verse eid="GAL 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="GAL 1:3" />Mfọn ye emem a-atooho Abasi Ete ye Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais aba ye ndufo. <verse eid="GAL 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="GAL 1:4" />Anye a-akeyaaha idem amọ anọ ke ntak mme idiọọkñkpọ ñnyịn nọ inyaaña ñnyịn esio ke idiọọk ayio emana ami, nte asañake akekem ke uduak Abasi Ete. <verse eid="GAL 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="GAL 1:5" />Ubọọñ anie anye ke nsi-nsi, nsi-nsi. Amen.<verse eid="GAL 1:5" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="s1">Eti Etob Mfen Ibaaha</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="GAL 1:6" />Añkpa miin idem eti-eti ke ndufo emesọsọp esịn anye a-akikoodo ndufo ke mfọn Krais ndin ekappa ekpañ utọñ enọ etob mfen, <verse eid="GAL 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="GAL 1:7" />i-imiidooho eti etob ke baaba usʌñ ndomokeed. Ami mmediọọñọ ke abañña mme awo e-edisịnne ndutịme ke esịd ndufo, sia ammọ enwana adibiabiat eti etob Krais. <verse eid="GAL 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="GAL 1:8" />Ado ñkọm akpedo ñnyịn, me enyere akpeto hefịn adikwọrọ eti etob mfen i-imiidooho se ñnyịn ikikwọrọ inọọ ndufo, yak ammọ eba ke isuuñọ Abasi! <verse eid="GAL 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="GAL 1:9" />Naña ñnyịn imaikitatañ, kpa ntoro ke ami mmaana ntañ: Adieke awo ndomokeed akwọrọke eti etob a-awuọhọ akpọñ se ndufo emaekenyịmme, yak ammọ eba ke isuuñọ Abasi!<verse eid="GAL 1:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="GAL 1:10" />Idahado me ami ñnwana adinem mme awo esịd me Abasi? Me ami ñnwana adinam esịd anem mme awo? Akpekedo ami ñkenwana adinem mme awo esịd, ami ñkpidooho isʌñutom Krais.<verse eid="GAL 1:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Abasi Ado Andikoot Pọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="GAL 1:11" />Nditọeka ke Krais, ami ñyem ndufo ediọọñọ ke eti etob a-ami ñkekwọrọke itooho awo. <verse eid="GAL 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="GAL 1:12" />Ami ñkibọọhọ anye nto awo ndomokeed, inyʌññọ ido nte ekeñkpeekpeep; ado ami ñkebọ anye nto adiyaara Yisọs Krais.<verse eid="GAL 1:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="GAL 1:13" />Sia ndufo emekop ebaña akaan eduuwem mmi ke idak edu ukpono Abasi mme Yuu, naña ami ñkesikọbọ ufọkabasi afai-afai ke afịd usʌñ ye naña ñkenwana adibiat anye. <verse eid="GAL 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="GAL 1:14" />Ami mmaadọọk ke idaha ke edu ukpono Abasi mme Yuu ñkan uwak mme Yuu e-ekedooho ubọk ñka mmi, ñnyʌñ nsịn idem eti-eti ke adisaña ke ndutʌm uwem mme eteete mmi. <verse eid="GAL 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="GAL 1:15" />Ado ke ini Abasi a-akensioho miin asaña-asaña anịm tọọñọ ke emana mmi, a-akenyʌññọ añkoot ke mfọn amọ, akenemme esịd <verse eid="GAL 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="GAL 1:16" />adiyaara Ayịn amọ ke idem mmi nọ ato do ami ñkwọrọ anye ke atu mme Gentile, ibọọrọ mmi akedo aditre adineme ye awo ndomokeed. <verse eid="GAL 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="GAL 1:17" />Ami ñkikaaha Yeruselem ñkekịt mbon e-ekembemme miin iso edo mme abọsịd, ado ñkesọọsọp ñkaa Arebia. Akema ami mmatịmme ñnyọñ Damaskọs.<verse eid="GAL 1:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="GAL 1:18" />Ke isua ita amaakeboiyo ami mmaadọọk ñkaa Yeruselem ñkediọọñọ Kefas<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Kefas awuọñọ Pita</char></note> ñnyʌñ ntie ye anye usen duob mme ition. <verse eid="GAL 1:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="GAL 1:19" />Ami ñkikịtte mme abọsịd mbon ñko, ibọhọke Yems, ayịneka Abọọñ ñnyịn. <verse eid="GAL 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="GAL 1:20" />Ami mmenwọñọ ke iso Abasi mbo ke afịd se ñwed ndomokeed idooho nsu.<verse eid="GAL 1:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="GAL 1:21" />Akema, mmaadika Siria ye Silisia. <verse eid="GAL 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="GAL 1:22" />Mme ufọkabasi ke Yudia e-ebaaha ke Krais ikindiọọñọke. <verse eid="GAL 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="GAL 1:23" />Ammọ ekekop etob kpọd, ete ke: “Awo a-akesikọbọke ñnyịn, idahami adikwọrọ mbuọdidem a-anye akenwanake adisobo.” <verse eid="GAL 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="GAL 1:24" />Ndin ammọ emaetooro Abasi ke ntak mmi.<verse eid="GAL 1:24" /></para>
  <chapter eid="GAL 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="GAL 2" />
  <para style="s1">Edat Pọọl Esịn ke atu mme Abọsịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="GAL 2:1" />Ke isua duob mme inaañ amaakeboiyo, ami mmaamaana ndọọk ñkaa Yeruselem, ini anyem ñkesaña ye Banabas ye Taitọs. <verse eid="GAL 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="GAL 2:2" />Ami ñkeka adinam uyio adiyaara añkebọọhọ nọ ato do mben eti etob a-ami ñkekwọrọke nnọ mme Gentile nnịm mme adaiwuod ke iso. Ami ñkenam ami mbaak adido ufeghe itọk mmi akedo ikpu-ikpu. <verse eid="GAL 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="GAL 2:3" />Kpayeado, ukpọk Taitọs a-akebaaha ye ami, awo ikibooho anye ke ana afọọrọ edʌd, akpesʌkado a-anye akedooho awo Greek. <verse eid="GAL 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="GAL 2:4" />Ñkpọ ami aketịppe sia mme nsu-nsu mbon i-imiinịmme ke akpanikọ emaesọọp edʌk atu ñnyịn adiyep ñkpọkñyak a-ñnyịn inieghe ke Krais Yisọs nọ ato do isịn ñnyịn ke ufʌn. <verse eid="GAL 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="GAL 2:5" />Ñnyịn ikiyaaha idem inọ ammọ ke usʌñ ndomokeed, nọ akpanikọ eti etob akpesʌhọ ye ndufo.<verse eid="GAL 2:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="GAL 2:6" />Amaado mbon e-ekenọọhọ asaña-asaña ukpono, se ammọ ekedodo iwuọñọke ñkpọ ndomokeed ke iso mmi; sia Abasi isatta awo ndomokeed. Ammọ ikidianna ñkpọ ndomokeed ke ukwọrọikọ mmi. Utu ke ado, ammọ emaediọọñọ ke ekeyaak ukwọrọ ikọ nnọọ mme Gentile ensịn miin ke ubọk, naña Pita akenie adikwọrọ nnọọ mme Yuu. <verse eid="GAL 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="GAL 2:7" />Ke akanna ado, ammọ emaedikịt ke emaennọ miin ubiọñutom adikwọrọ eti etob nnọọ mbon i-imiidiọọñọke Abasi<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho mbon Gentile</char></note>, kpa naña ekenọọ Pita akekwọrọ anọ mbon e-emaekefọọrọ edʌd<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho mbon Yuu; se ñko ke Kalesia 2:11 ye 14</char></note>. <verse eid="GAL 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="GAL 2:8" />Sia Abasi a-akebaaha ye Pita ke utom ammọ nte abọsịd mme Yuu, mbon e-efọọrọke edʌd, akenyʌñ aba ye ami ke utom mmi nte abọsịd mme Gentile. <verse eid="GAL 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="GAL 2:9" />Yems, Kefas ye Yọọn, e-ekedoññoke mme adaaha emaikọọm ñnyịn ubọk adinyịmme ke ami ye Banabas ñko ido mme abọsịd ke ammọ emaekekịt mfọn A-Abasi akennọọhọ miin. Ammọ emaenyịmme ebo yak ñnyịn ibịne mme Gentile, ke ini ammọ ebịneke mbon e-efọọrọke edʌd. <verse eid="GAL 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="GAL 2:10" />Ukweeñe se ammọ ekibeeñe ñnyịn akedo yak ika iso itoiyo mbon uweene, a-adooho ñkpọ a-ami ñkenieghe udọñ adinam afịd ini.<verse eid="GAL 2:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Asua Anọ Kefas</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="GAL 2:11" />Ke ini Kefas amaakedi Antiọk, ami mmaanie ntuaaha ye anye iso ye iso, sia anye akeba ke ubiomikpe. <verse eid="GAL 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="GAL 2:12" />Sia mbemiso mbon a-Yems akesiooho adọñ ekedisịm, anye amaasidia ñkpọ ye mme Gentile, ado ke ammọ emaekedisịm anye amaatọọñọ adisịkke nda ñnyʌñ mbakka idem amọ ñkpọñ mme Gentile, sia anye akebaak mbon e-ekesịneke ke atu mbon e-efọọrọke edʌd. <verse eid="GAL 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="GAL 2:13" />Mme Yuu mfen emaekeene anye ebakka eda ke unam utom anyen awo, ndin amaato ke ntak ami, emaenam Banabas ñko awakka akpọñ usʌñ.<verse eid="GAL 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="GAL 2:14" />Ke ini ami ñkekịtte ke ammọ ikinamma ñkpọ nọ akekem ye akpanikọ eti etob Abasi, ami mmaabo Kefas ke iso afịd ammọ nte: “Afo ado awo Yuu, ado afo adu uwem nte Gentile, uduuho nte Yuu. Nsinam nọ afo abo ke ana mme Gentile ekeene esaña ke eduuwem mme Yuu?<verse eid="GAL 2:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="GAL 2:15" />“Ñnyịn se ido mme Yuu ke emana, i-imiidooho mme anam idiọọkñkpọ nte mme Gentile, <verse eid="GAL 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="GAL 2:16" />imidiọọñọ ke ikpe itoppoke awo ikeene adinịm mbed, ado ato mbuọdidem ke Yisọs Krais. Ke ntoro, ñnyịn ñko imikọọñ mbuọdidem ñnyịn ke Krais Yisọs nọ ñnyịn inie utoppo ikpe ke Krais, idooho ke adinịm mbed, sia awo ndomokeed idiibọọhọ utoppo ikpe ito adinịm mbed.<verse eid="GAL 2:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="GAL 2:17" />“Ado adieke ñnyịn, ke adinwana adibọ utoppo ikpe ke Krais, ñnyịn i-idoññoke Yuu ikịt ke ñnyịn idoñño mme anam idiọọkñkpọ, nte ado iwọttọ ke Krais adadaara idiọọkñkpọ? Idooho ntoro ke baaba usʌñ ndomokeed! <verse eid="GAL 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="GAL 2:18" />Adieke ami mmaanake mbọp se mmaakewuut, mmenam ediọọñọ ke ami ndo abiad mbed.<verse eid="GAL 2:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="GAL 2:19" />“Sia ke ntak mbed ke ami ñkekpa nnọ mbed nọ ato do ami ndu uwem nnọ Abasi. <verse eid="GAL 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="GAL 2:20" />Emaeñkọñ miin ye Krais ndin idooho ami ndu uwem aba, ado Krais adu uwem ke idem mmi. Idahami, uwem a-ami nduuho ke abʌkidem, ndu ke mbuọdidem ke Ayịn Abasi, a-akemmaaha miin anyʌñ ayaak idem amọ annọ miin. <verse eid="GAL 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="GAL 2:21" />Ami nnəkko mfọn Abasi nnịm ñkañ keed, sia adieke ekpebọọhọ adinenido eto mbed, akpewuọñọ ke ñkpa Krais akedo utak-utak!”<verse eid="GAL 2:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="GAL 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="GAL 3" />
  <para style="s1">Mbuọdidem me Utom Mbed</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="GAL 3:1" />Ndufo ndisịme mbon Kalesia! Anie ikifʌk ndufo ñkịm ke anyen? Emaenekke eben Yisọs Krais e-ekọññọ ke krọs iwọt ndufo. <verse eid="GAL 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="GAL 3:2" />Ami ñkpaama adikpeep ñkpọ keed kpọd ito ndufo. Ndufo ekebọ adisana Sịbidịd eto adinịm mbed me adinịm se ekekop? <verse eid="GAL 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="GAL 3:3" />Ado nte ndufo emenekke esịme? Ke imaikitọọñọ ye Sịbidịd, nte eyem adikama abʌkidem ñkweeñe se eketọọñọ? <verse eid="GAL 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="GAL 3:4" />Nte afịd ufen ndufo akappa ado utak-utak, adieke akedooho utak-utak ke akpanikọ? <verse eid="GAL 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="GAL 3:5" />Isọñ ida ise, nte Abasi inọ ndufo Sịbidịd, amaana anam mme utịppeñkpọ ke atu ndufo sia emenam utom mbed me sia emenịm se ekekop? <verse eid="GAL 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="GAL 3:6" />Ebraham ñko “amaanịm Abasi ke akpanikọ, ndin emaebat enọ anye nte adinenido.”<verse eid="GAL 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="GAL 3:7" />Yak inwaña ndufo ndin ke mbon e-enieghe mbuọdidem edoñño nditọ Ebraham. <verse eid="GAL 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="GAL 3:8" />Ikọ Abasi amaada akịt ke Abasi ayaatoppo mme Gentile ikpe ke mbuọdidem, ndin anye amaabem iso asuan etob ado anọ Ebraham ate: “Afịd mme idịd eyaebọ adidiọñ uto fiin.” <verse eid="GAL 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="GAL 3:9" />Ke ntoro e-ediọñ mbon e-enieghe mbuọdidem edian ye Ebraham, a-adooho awo mbuọdidem.<verse eid="GAL 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="GAL 3:10" />Afịd mbon e-edotto anyen ke edinịm mbed eba ke idak isuuñọ, sia e-ewet: “Adọdiọọk anọ afịd mbon i-imiikaaha iso inam se iwere ke Ñwed Mbed.” <verse eid="GAL 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="GAL 3:11" />Ado awọt anwa-anwa ke awo ndomokeed inieghe utoppo ikpe ke iso Abasi ito mbed, sia, “mme ndinen awo ediidu uwem ke mbuọdidem.” <verse eid="GAL 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="GAL 3:12" />Mbed ikọñọke ke mbuọdidem, utu ke ado, anye abo, “Awo a-anamma mme ñkpọ ami adiidu uwem ikeene mme ñkpọ ami.” <verse eid="GAL 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="GAL 3:13" />Krais amaifak ñnyịn asio ke isuuñọ mbed ke anye adikikappa ndo isuuñọ inọọ ñnyịn, sia e-ewet ebo, “Adọdiọọk anọ awo akeedodo e-ekọññọ ke eto.” <verse eid="GAL 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="GAL 3:14" />Anye akifak ñnyịn nọ ato do mme adidiọñ e-ekenọọhọ Ebraham akanna abịne mme Gentile ato ke Krais Yisọs, nọ ato ke mbuọdidem ñnyịn ibọ enwọñọ a-Sịbidịd.<verse eid="GAL 3:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mbed ye Enwọñọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="GAL 3:15" />Nditọeka ke Krais, yak ami ndat uwọdñkpọ nto edu uwem ke usen ke usen. Kpa naña awo ndomokeed imiikemeke adituut nnịm me adidian ñkpọ ke edioomo ubon awo a-amaakebaba, anyʌñ ado ntoro ke ñkpọ ami. <verse eid="GAL 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="GAL 3:16" />Emaetatañ mme enwọñọ ami enọ Ebraham ye mme mfịd idịb amọ. Ñwed Abasi ibooho, “ye mme mfịd,” a-awuọñọke uwak awo, ado abo “ye mfịd mfo” a-adooho Krais. <verse eid="GAL 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="GAL 3:17" />Se ami ntañ awuọñọ ntom: Mbed e-ebenne edi ke mme isua ikie inaañ mme edịb mme duob (430) emaekeboiyo, isịkke isio edioomo A-Abasi amaakenanam, inyʌññọ itop enwọñọ ado iduọọk. <verse eid="GAL 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="GAL 3:18" />Sia, adieke udiaakpa akọñọke ke mbed, awuọñọ ke anye ikọñọke aba ke enwọñọ; ado Abasi ke mfọn amọ akeyaak anye anọ Ebraham ato enwọñọ.<verse eid="GAL 3:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="GAL 3:19" />Nsoo ido ntak ndin e-ekenọọhọ mbed? Ekedian anye ke ntak ndiọiñkpọ tutu mfịd e-ekenwọñọke enọ adi. Ekenọ mbed ke ubọk mme enyere ndin eyaak enọ atie ubiọñ. <verse eid="GAL 3:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="GAL 3:20" />Atieubiọñ isibaaha inọ ñkañ keed kpọd; ado Abasi ado keed.<verse eid="GAL 3:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="GAL 3:21" />Ke ntoro, ado nte mbed a-anie ntuaha ye mme enwọñọ Abasi? Nwaaña nsa-o! Sia akpedo emaenọ mbed a-akpekekanna anọ uwem, adinenido akpeketo mbed ado. <verse eid="GAL 3:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="GAL 3:22" />Ado ñwed Abasi asịn afịd ñkpọ ke ñkpakọb idiọọkñkpọ, nọ ato do se emaekenwọñọ, e-ekenọọhọ ato mbuọdidem ke Yisọs Krais, ekeme iyaak nnọọ mbon e-enịmme ke akpanikọ.<verse eid="GAL 3:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Nditọ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="GAL 3:23" />Mbemiso mbuọdidem akedidi, ñnyịn ikisịne ke ñkpakọb ke idak mbed, e-ekikọppọ ñnyịn enịm tutu ediyaara mbuọdidem. <verse eid="GAL 3:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="GAL 3:24" />Ke ntoro ekenịm mbed nọ idat ñnyịn usʌñ asọk Krais, nọ itoppo ñnyịn ikpe ke mbuọdidem. <verse eid="GAL 3:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="GAL 3:25" />Idahami sia mbuọdidem amaakedi, ñnyịn ibaaha aba ke idak mbed.<verse eid="GAL 3:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="GAL 3:26" />Ke ntoro ke Krais Yisọs afịd ndufo edoñño nditọ Abasi ato ke mbuọdidem, <verse eid="GAL 3:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="GAL 3:27" />sia afịd ndufo e-emaekeduọk mmọọñ isịn ke Krais emeben Krais esịne ke idem. <verse eid="GAL 3:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="GAL 3:28" />Yuu me Gentile, me afʌn me amanaisọñ ibaaha, awodeen me awonwaan inyʌññọ iba, sia afịd ndufo edo keed ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="GAL 3:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="GAL 3:29" />Adieke adooho Krais inie ndufo, awuọ ndufo edo mfịd Ebraham, enyʌñ edo mme adiaakpa ato ke enwọñọ.<verse eid="GAL 3:29" /></para>
  <chapter eid="GAL 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="GAL 4" />
  <para style="s1">Ndufo Edo Nditọ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="GAL 4:1" />Se ami ntañ ado ke ini adiaakpa asʌkkọ ado etəkayịn, anye aba nte afʌn, akpesʌkado a-anye anieghe afịd se ete akekpa akpọñ. <verse eid="GAL 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="GAL 4:2" />Ana anye asịne ke idak ukara ye andikama anye ye mbon se ekeyaak afịd ñkpọ esịn ke ubọk tutu ini se ete amọ akenịm adikem. <verse eid="GAL 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="GAL 4:3" />Kpa ntoro ñko, ke idaha a-ñnyịn ikidoññoke ntəkayịn, ikibañña ke ufʌn ke idak mme sịbidịd mbed ukara ederimbod. <verse eid="GAL 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="GAL 4:4" />Ado ke ini amaakedikem ayọhọ-ayọhọ, Abasi amaadọñ Ayịn amọ a-akemanake ato awonwaan, amana ke idak mbed, <verse eid="GAL 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="GAL 4:5" />nọ adifakka mbon e-ebaaha ke idak mbed, nọ ñnyịn ikan ibọ ayọhọ unen nditọ. <verse eid="GAL 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="GAL 4:6" />Sia ndufo edoññoke nditọ, Abasi amaasịn Sịbidịd Ayịn ke esịd, Sịbidịd a-asioho uyio akoot “<char style="tl">Abba,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Abba </char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọñọ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ete </char><char style="ft" closed="false">ke usem Aramaik</char></note> Ete.” <verse eid="GAL 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="GAL 4:7" />Ke ntoro, afo udooho aba afʌn, ado Ayịn, ndin sia afo adooho Ayịn, Abasi unam fiin ado adiaakpa ñko.<verse eid="GAL 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl a-Anie Eyịghe Abaña Mbon Kalesia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="GAL 4:8" />Ke mme usen edem, ke ini a-ndufo imiikidiọọñọke Abasi, ndufo ekedoñño ifʌn enọ mme ñkpọ i-imiidoññoke abasi. <verse eid="GAL 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="GAL 4:9" />Ado idahami, a-ndufo ediọọñọke Abasi, ke adinekke ntañ, akap ado Abasi idiọọñọ ndufo, nsoo inam nọ ndufo ekanna edem emaana ebịne mme ntək sịbidịd ye mme ubonoñkpọ adudu i-imiiwuọñọke ñkpọ ndomokeed? Nte ndufo eyem ammọ emaana isịn ndufo ke ufʌn? <verse eid="GAL 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="GAL 4:10" />Ndufo esʌk enaanam mme ndutʌm e-ebañake mme asaña-asana usen, mme afiọñ, mme ini ye mme isua. <verse eid="GAL 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="GAL 4:11" />Ndịk annam miin ibaña ndufo, sia adiba nte afịd ufen mmi ke idem ndufo ababaha.<verse eid="GAL 4:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="GAL 4:12" />Nditọeka ke Krais, ami mmikpe ndufo ubọk, ikappa iba nte ami, sia ami mmaakappa mba nte ndufo. Ndufo ikinnamma miin idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="GAL 4:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="GAL 4:13" />Nte ndufo ediọọñọke, aketo ke ntak udọñọ ikpọkidem ke ami ñkebemiso ñkwọrọ ikọ inọọ ndufo ke akpa ifed. <verse eid="GAL 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="GAL 4:14" />Akpesʌkado u-udọñọ mmi akedooho ñkpọ idomo inọọ ndufo, ndufo ikiinsọọnọ miin, utu ke ado, emaedaara adidi mmi nte ñkedo enyere Abasi, me Krais Yisọs ke idem amọ. <verse eid="GAL 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="GAL 4:15" />Inemesịd a-ndufo ekenieghe ennọ miin aba mọọ idahami? Ami mmekeme itie ntiense mbo ke ndufo ekpaekekappa anyen ndufo esio ennọ miin, adieke ekpekekanna enam ntoro. <verse eid="GAL 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="GAL 4:16" />Nte ami mmekappa ndo asua ndufo ke edidọkkọ ndufo akpanikọ?<verse eid="GAL 4:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="GAL 4:17" />Mbon e-ekwọrọke nsu-nsu etob inọọ ndufo esịn ifịk nọ ato do idʌt ndufo enọ idem ammọ, ado idooho ke eti. Se ammọ eyem ado adidiañña ndufo ikpọñ ñnyịn, nọ ato do ndufo eyaak idem ndufo afịd-afịd enọ ammọ. <verse eid="GAL 4:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="GAL 4:18" />Anekke afọn adisịn ifịk afịd-afịd ini, adieke adooho ke eti ntak, ñnyʌñ nnam ntoro afịd-afịd ini, idooho ke ini ami mbaaha ye ndufo kpọd. <verse eid="GAL 4:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="GAL 4:19" />Ndima nditọ mmi, a-ami nsʌkkọ mba ke ubiak uman nnọ tutu Krais aboiyo adʌk esịd ndufo, <verse eid="GAL 4:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="GAL 4:20" />ubaha nte ami ñkpebaaha ye ndufo idahami ñnyʌñ ñkpʌhọ uyio mmi, sia idem a-anekke añkpa miin ibaña ndufo.<verse eid="GAL 4:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Haka ye Sera</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="GAL 4:21" />Indọkọ miin, ndufo e-eyemme adiba ke idak mbed, ndufo idiọọñọke se mbed atañ? <verse eid="GAL 4:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="GAL 4:22" />Sia e-ewet ebo ke Ebraham akenie nditọ ideen iba, keed akemana ato afʌn awonwaan, anye ako akemana ato amanaisọñ awonwaan. <verse eid="GAL 4:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="GAL 4:23" />Ayịn a-afʌn awonwaan akemana akeene usʌñ abʌkidem; ado ayịn a-aketooho amanaisọñ awonwaan akemana akeene enwọñọ Abasi.<verse eid="GAL 4:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="GAL 4:24" />Edat mme ñkpọ ami nte ñke, sia mme ibaan ami eda enọ edioomo iba. Edioomo keed ato Abod Sainai anyʌñ aman nditọ e-ediidoñño ifʌn: Anye ami ado Haka. <verse eid="GAL 4:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="GAL 4:25" />Ndin Haka ada anọ Abod Sainai ke Arebia a-anyʌññọ aba nte abio Yeruselem abio mfịn, sia anye asịne ke ufʌn ye nditọ amọ. <verse eid="GAL 4:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="GAL 4:26" />Ado Yeruselem a-abaaha ke anyọñ idooho afʌn, ndin anye ado eka ñnyịn. <verse eid="GAL 4:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="GAL 4:27" />Sia e-ewewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="GAL 4:27">“Nem esịd, awonwaan ada,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="GAL 4:27">afo a-adooho kpaanam umanna ayịn:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="GAL 4:27">Sio ñkpo idaara nyʌñ bọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="GAL 4:27">afo a-adooho kpaanam ukoppo ubiak uman;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="GAL 4:27">sia nditọ ikpọọñ awonwaan</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="GAL 4:27">ewak ekan nditọ adọ ebe.”<verse eid="GAL 4:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="GAL 4:28" />Idahami ndufo, nditọeka mmi ke Krais, kpa nte Aisik, ndufo edoñño nditọ enwọñọ. <verse eid="GAL 4:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="GAL 4:29" />Ke ini ado ayịn a-akemanake ato abʌkidem amaatʌkkọ ayịn a-akemanake ato adudu Sịbidịd. Asʌk ado ntoro tutu idahami. <verse eid="GAL 4:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="GAL 4:30" />Ado nsoo ke ñwed Abasi atañ? “Bịne afʌn awonwaan ado ye ayịn amọ sio, sia ayịn afʌn awonwaan ado idiiwanake ke udeeme ñkpọ adiaakpa ye ayịn amanaisọñ awonwaan.” <verse eid="GAL 4:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="GAL 4:31" />Ke ntoro, nditọeka ke Krais, ñnyịn idooho nditọ afʌn awonwaan, ido nditọ amanaisọñ awonwaan.<verse eid="GAL 4:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="GAL 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="GAL 5" />
  <para style="s1">Ñkpọkñyak ke Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="GAL 5:1" />Ke ntak adinam ñnyịn ido mme nditọ amanaisọñ ke Krais akisịññe ñnyịn ke ufʌn. Isọọñọ ida, ndin, ikiimaana iben akpọnọ ufʌn ikọñọ.<verse eid="GAL 5:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="GAL 5:2" />Iwet ikọ mmi inịm! Ami, Pọọl, mbo ke imaiyak ifọọrọ ndufo edʌd, Krais idiibaaha ufọn ndomokeed inọ ndufo aba. <verse eid="GAL 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="GAL 5:3" />Mmemaana ntañ, awo a-ayaaha idem amọ anọ yak efọọrọ edʌd ana anịm afịd mbed. <verse eid="GAL 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="GAL 5:4" />Emaidiañña ndufo e-enwanake adibọ utoppo ikpe nto mbed ekpọñ Krais; ndufo emewuọ ekpọñ mfọn Abasi. <verse eid="GAL 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="GAL 5:5" />Sia ato ke Sịbidịd ye ke mbuọdidem ke ñnyịn itie ibet adinenido a-ñnyịn idotto anyen. <verse eid="GAL 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="GAL 5:6" />Sia ke Krais Yisọs adifọọrọ edʌd me aditre adifọọrọ edʌd iwuọñọke ñkpọ ndomokeed. Ñkukweeñe ñkpọ a-abaaha ufọn, ado mbuọdidem a-awọttọ idem ke ima.<verse eid="GAL 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="GAL 5:7" />Ndufo ekefeghe eti itọk. Anie awo ikikpịkke ndufo iso ibo ikiinam se ido akpanikọ? <verse eid="GAL 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="GAL 5:8" />Utọ ndukpek ado itooho anye i-ikoodo ndufo. <verse eid="GAL 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="GAL 5:9" />“Etək yiis asinam afịd eboho uyo atịt.” <verse eid="GAL 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="GAL 5:10" />Ami mmenekke nnie isọñesịd ke Abọọñ mbo, ke ndufo idiikereke ke usʌñ mfen. Awo akeedodo i-itoppo ndufo asịn ke ndutịme ayaabọ ufen. <verse eid="GAL 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="GAL 5:11" />Nditọeka ke Krais, adieke adooho ami nsʌk ñkwọrọ ufọọrọ edʌd, ntak e-esʌkkọ eñkọbọ miin-e? Ke ntoro e-eben ndudue a-atooho krọs efep. <verse eid="GAL 5:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="GAL 5:12" />Amaado mme andisịn ndutịme, ami ñkpaama ammọ ekpok idem ammọ ke ikwa akan ufọọrọ edʌd kpọd!<verse eid="GAL 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Uwem ke Sịbidịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="GAL 5:13" />Ekikoot ndufo, nditọeka ke Krais, ebo ewuọñọ ke ufʌn. Ado ikiiyak uwuọufʌn ndufo anam nọ ndufo edʌk enyịne ke utom abʌkidem; utu ke ado, inam ñkpọ inọ emọ-emọ ke nsuukidem ye ima. <verse eid="GAL 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="GAL 5:14" />Sia afịd mbed akọñọ ke mbed keed ami kpọd: “Ma mbọhọidʌñ mfo nte idem mfo.” <verse eid="GAL 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="GAL 5:15" />Adieke ndufo ekaaha iso ke adidom ñnyʌñ nta emọ-emọ, ikpeme, miidooho ntoro ndufo eyaesobo emọ-emọ.<verse eid="GAL 5:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="GAL 5:16" />Ke ntoro, ami ibo ndufo, isaña ke Sịbidịd, ndin ndufo idiinọọhọ mme udọñ abʌkidem uyʌkkọ. <verse eid="GAL 5:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="GAL 5:17" />Sia abʌkidem ayem se Sịbidịd imiimaaha, ndin Sịbidịd inyʌññọ iwʌrọ se abʌkidem ama. Naña ammọ iba enwanwana ye idem ammọ, ke ntoro afo ukanna unam se akpeyem adinam. <verse eid="GAL 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="GAL 5:18" />Ado adieke Sịbidịd udatta fiin usʌñ, afo ubaaha ke idak mbed.<verse eid="GAL 5:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="GAL 5:19" />Mme utom abʌkidem ewuọñọ eda anwa-anwa: Use, efịbe, ndedeghe uwem, akpọsọñ udia uwem; <verse eid="GAL 5:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="GAL 5:20" />ukpono ndem ye ifọd; usua, ntịme, ufịb, akpọsọñ ifiobesịd, idiọọk udọñ, unana ndukoppo, ubakka <verse eid="GAL 5:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="GAL 5:21" />ye isịnanyen, ukpa mmịn, akpọsọñ udia uwem ye mme ndiọi uwem mfen. Ami mmetañ inọ ndufo nte mmaaketatañ ke mbon e-eduuho utọ uwem ami idiidʌkkọ abioubọọñ Abasi.<verse eid="GAL 5:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="GAL 5:22" />Ado mfịd Sịbidịd ado ima, idadesịd, emem, ime, mfọnido, eti uwem, mbuọdidem, <verse eid="GAL 5:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="GAL 5:23" />ifuuro-ifuuro ido ye mfadidem. Mbed ndomokeed ibiọọñọke mme ñkpọ ntoro. <verse eid="GAL 5:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="GAL 5:24" />Mbon e-ebaaha ke Krais Yisọs emaekọñ abʌkidem ye afịd nduwʌrọ ye idiọọk itọñ ammọ ke krọs. <verse eid="GAL 5:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="GAL 5:25" />Sia ñnyịn iduuho ke Sịbidịd, yak ñnyịn isaña ke Sịbidịd. <verse eid="GAL 5:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="GAL 5:26" />Yak ñnyịn ikiikịt idem, inam esịd ayat emọ-emọ inyʌñ inie ufịb ye emọ-emọ awo.<verse eid="GAL 5:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="GAL 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="GAL 6" />
  <para style="s1">Adinam se Ifọn Nnọọ Afịd Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="GAL 6:1" />Nditọeka ke Krais, adieke emʌmmọ awo ke idiọọkñkpọ, ndufo e-esʌkkọ eba ke Sịbidịd akpena ebenne anye edot ke itie amọ. Ado, ndufo ke idem ndufo ikpeme, miidooho ndufo ñko emekeme edinyʌñ ndʌk idomo. <verse eid="GAL 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="GAL 6:2" />Ibiom mbiomo emọ-emọ, ndin ke utọ usʌñ ami eyaenam mbed Krais ayọhọ-ayọhọ. <verse eid="GAL 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="GAL 6:3" />Adieke awo ndomokeed akereke ke imọ iminie se ido, ke ini anye miidooho ñkpọ ndomokeed, anye abiaña idem amọ. <verse eid="GAL 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="GAL 6:4" />Akpena awo keedekeed adomo adinam amọ ase. Ndin ammọ ekeme adikokko idem, ibenne idem ammọ ikidomo ye mbon mfen, <verse eid="GAL 6:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="GAL 6:5" />sia ana awo keedekeed abiom mbiomo amọ. <verse eid="GAL 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="GAL 6:6" />Kpayeado, awo a-abọọhọ ukpeeb ke ikọ Abasi ana awana afịd nti ñkpọ ye mme andikpeeb anye.<verse eid="GAL 6:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="GAL 6:7" />Ikiiyak awo ibiaña ndufo, awo ikemeke adikama Abasi ntọ ndọk. Se awo atọ, kpa ado ke adọk. <verse eid="GAL 6:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="GAL 6:8" />Awo atọọhọ asịn ke inemesịd abʌkidem, ayaadọk nsobo ato abʌkidem; anye atọọhọ asịn ke inemesịd Sịbidịd, ayaadọk nsi-nsi uwem ato Sịbidịd. <verse eid="GAL 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="GAL 6:9" />Yak ñnyịn ikuukpa mba ke adinam eti ñkpọ, sia ini amaakem iyaidọk mfịd nti utom ñnyịn, adieke ñnyịn isọọñọke ida ikisịm utịd. <verse eid="GAL 6:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="GAL 6:10" />Ke ntoro, naña ñnyịn ikpikakan yak inam se ifọn inọ afịd awo, akpan-akpan mbon e-esịneke ke ubon mbon e-enịmme ke akpanikọ.<verse eid="GAL 6:10" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="s1">Adimana Ufa A-akpon Akan Adifọọrọ Edʌd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="GAL 6:11" />Ise utọ ñkpoon abiisi a-ami ñkamake iwet ndufo ñwedetob ke ubọk mmi!<verse eid="GAL 6:11" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="GAL 6:12" />Mbon e-eyemme adinam utom anyen awo ke abʌkidem enwana adinam ndufo efọọrọ edʌd. Ukweeñe ntak a-ammọ enamma ami ado nọ ebọkkọ ndutʌhọ ke ntak krọs Krais. <verse eid="GAL 6:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="GAL 6:13" />Idooho nte ebo ke mbon e-efọọrọke edʌd enịm mbed, kpayeado ammọ eyem ndufo efọọrọ edʌd nọ ato do ammọ enam inua ebaña ikpọkidem ndufo. <verse eid="GAL 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="GAL 6:14" />Abasi idiiyakka ami nnam inua ibọhọke ke krọs Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais, a-atooho ke anye ekọñ ederimbod ke idem mmi, enyʌñ eñkọñ miin ke abaña ederimbod. <verse eid="GAL 6:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="GAL 6:15" />Adifọọrọ edʌd me aditre adifọọrọ edʌd iwuọñọke ñkpọ ndomokeed; ukweeñe se iwuọñọ ñkpọ ado adimana ndʌk ufa uwem. <verse eid="GAL 6:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="GAL 6:16" />Yak emem ye mbọm asịm afịd mbon e-ekeeneke mbed ami, kpa Isrel ake Abasi.<verse eid="GAL 6:16" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="GAL 6:17" />Tọọñọ ke idahami kaa iso, ke awo ndomokeed amfịna miin aba, sia ami ñkama mme idiọọñọ mbọn Yisọs ke idem mmi.<verse eid="GAL 6:17" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="GAL 6:18" />Nditọeka mmi ke Krais, yak mfọn Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais aba ye sịbidịd ndufo. Amen.<verse eid="GAL 6:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="GAL 6" />
</usx>